Package: podman
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://podman.io
Description: Manage pods, containers and container images (built from source)
 Podman is a daemonless container engine for developing, managing and running
 OCI containers and pods.
 .
 This is NOT the distribution package. It is built from the upstream
 v@UPSTREAM_VERSION@ release tag and targeted at Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy), where the
 distribution ships only podman 3.4.4. See the packaging notes in the source
 repository for why the 4.9.x series is the newest that jammy can run.
 .
 Build tags used: seccomp, systemd, apparmor, excluding the btrfs and
 devicemapper graph drivers.
# Runtime dependencies, in three groups:
#   1. container tooling jammy already provides (conmon is version-floored
#      because jammy's 2.0.25 predates what podman 4.x expects)
#   2. shared libraries the pinned build tags link against -- these correspond
#      one-to-one with BUILDTAGS in scripts/20-build-podman.sh
#   3. base system libraries
Depends: conmon (>= 2.1.0),
         crun | runc,
         containernetworking-plugins,
         iptables,
         tzdata,
         libapparmor1,
         libc6 (>= 2.34),
         libgcc-s1,
         libgpgme11 (>= 1.4.1),
         libseccomp2 (>= 2.5.0),
         libsqlite3-0,
         libsystemd0
Recommends: buildah,
            catatonit,
            fuse-overlayfs,
            slirp4netns,
            uidmap
Suggests: podman-docker
# No Conflicts on the distro podman: this package *replaces* it, and a Conflicts
# without a matching Replaces would make the upgrade fail outright.
Replaces: podman
Provides: podman
